          %p
            Since full embeddings are injective on objects, “being tight” is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stuff%2C+structure%2C+property"} property
            of a loose morphism. (This would still be true in the “up to unique isomorphism” sense even if we did not ask for injectivity on objects, but when dealing with strict things, it is easier to keep them as strict as possible.) And since full embeddings are fully faithful, the 2-cells between two tight morphisms are the same whether we regard them as tight or as loose.
          %p
