            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℱ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{F}
            to consist of fully faithful functors, with squares that commute up to specified isomorphism, and then by considering
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℱ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{F}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+bicategories"} enriched bicategories
            rather than enriched categories. Such a thing would be equivalent to an identity-on-objects and locally-fully-faithful pseudofunctor between bicategories.
          %p One could consider semi-strict versions as well, in which (for example) the tight morphisms form a strict 2-category.
